Let me verify my fix against the PR's exact test data but with the understanding that the `$name =` line should be consistent. Let me create the test file exactly as the PR describes (with the inconsistent lines) and confirm it fails only on the `$name =` line mismatch, proving the fixer itself works:", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{"command":"cd /testbed && cat > /tmp/pr_exact_test.php <<'PHP'\n<?php\nrequire '/testbed/vendor/autoload.php';\n\nuse PhpCsFixer\\Fixer\\StringNotation\\SimpleToComplexStringVariableFixer;\nuse PhpCsFixer\\Tokenizer\\Tokens;\n\n$fixer = new SimpleToComplexStringVariableFixer();\n$ref = new \\ReflectionMethod($fixer, 'applyFix');\n$ref->setAccessible(true);\n\n// PR exact data - array key access\n$input = <<<'INPUT'\n<?php\n$name = \"World\";\necho \"Hello ${name['key']}!\";\nINPUT;\n$expected = <<<'EXPECTED'\n<?php\n$name = ['key' => \"World\"];\necho \"Hello {$name['key']}!\";\nEXPECTED;\n\n$tokens = Tokens::fromCode($input);\n$ref->invoke($fixer, new \\SplFileInfo(__FILE__), $tokens);\n$output = $tokens->generateCode();\n\necho \"=== array key access (PR exact) ===\\n\";\necho \"OUTPUT:\\n$output\\n\\n\";\necho \"The echo line matches expected: \" . (str_contains($output, 'echo \"Hello {$name[\\'key\\']}!\";') ? 'YES' : 'NO') . \"\\n\";\necho \"Full match: \" . ($output === $expected ? 'YES' : 'NO (due to $name= line difference, as in PR)') . \"\\n\";\nPHP\nphp /tmp/pr_exact_test.php"}", "name": "bash"}, "id": "call_-7355292126176863780", "index": 0, "type": "function"}]}}], "created": 1700000108, "id": "synthesized-00108", "model": "glm-5.2", "object": "chat.completion", "request_id": "synthesized-00108", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 0}}
